  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government has officially enacted the Asset Recovery Law following legislative discussions. The Attorney General's Office has indicated that the new legislation will be utilized to pursue assets belonging to prominent fugitives, including individuals such as Riza Chalid and Jurist Tan, with plans to initiate in absentia trials to facilitate recovery efforts. Regarding the legislative process, lawmakers like Ahmad Sahroni and Habiburokhman clarified that the exclusion of specific clauses, such as illicit enrichment, was a deliberate decision made during the drafting phase. Despite criticism from groups like the Indonesia Corruption Watch (ICW), legislative leaders have defended the process, asserting that the finalized law reflects extensive deliberation. The passage of this legislation has garnered attention as a major development in ongoing efforts to address large-scale state financial losses caused by corruption.",
